<title>LEBANON: All weeklu Lebanese t-bill yields fall.</title>
<headline>All weeklu Lebanese t-bill yields fall.</headline>
<dateline>BEIRUT 1997-03-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>All yields fell on Lebanese treasury bills, according to weekly rates issued by the Bank of Lebanon on Monday.</p>
<p>It announced the following interest rates for its March 13 issues (previous week in brackets):</p>
<p>    Term		     Discount		     Yield</p>
<p>				(percent)		   (percent)</p>
<p>    Three months	  13.36 (13.38)	     13.82 (13.84)</p>
<p>    Six months	    13.57 (13.59)	     14.55 (14.58)</p>
<p>    12 months	     13.20 (13.23)	     15.20 (15.24)</p>
<p>    24 months   (Interest payable twice yearly) 16.08 (16.12)</p>
<p>-Beirut editorial (961 1) 602057 745307 745308</p>
</text>
